# Line endings are settled here rather than left to each machine's core.autocrlf.
#
# Everything committed is already LF — `git ls-files --eol` reports i/lf for all 2563 tracked
# text files — but Windows checkouts were getting CRLF working copies, which made
# `npm run format:check` report 2340 failures locally against CI's 1177. Half of that number was
# line endings alone, and any Windows developer running `npm run format` would have rewritten the
# whole repository in CRLF (LA-63).
#
# `eol=lf` fixes the working tree too, so prettier's default endOfLine and CI agree with what a
# developer sees locally.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows shells are the one place CRLF is not cosmetic — a .bat read with LF endings can break.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Never touched, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.node binary
*.dll binary
*.exe binary
